DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     With no argument, ddaattee prints the current date and time,
     followed by the time zone name.

     With a numeric argument, ddaattee sets the system's date and
     time (only the superuser may do this) and then prints the
     result exactly as it would with no argument.  The argument
     gives, from the right, the minute and hour (_m_m and _h_h, both
     required), and optionally the day of month, month, and last
     two digits of the year (_d_d, _m_m, _y_y), each optional and taken
     two digits at a time working leftward; any of the optional
     leading fields that are omitted are left at their current
     value.  A seconds field (._s_s) may follow the minutes field.
     ddaattee refuses to set an impossible date, such as day 32 of a
     month, or a month that has fewer days than the given day of
     month allows.

     -uu   Print and, if setting the time, interpret the argument
          in Greenwich Mean Time instead of the local time zone.

     When it sets the time, ddaattee also records the change in
     /uussrr/aaddmm/wwttmmpp and adjusts the modification time of
     /eettcc/bboooottttiimmee so that the recorded system-up-since time
     stays consistent across the change.

