DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     ddaattee prints a usage message and exits with status 1 if given
     an option other than -uu, more than one non-option argument,
     an argument whose minute or hour field is not two digits, or
     a day of month that does not exist in the given (or current)
     month.  It also exits with status 1, after printing ``No
     permission'', if a non-superuser tries to set the time.

NNOOTTEESS
     Only the superuser can change the system's date or time.

     ddaattee builds its printed output from the C library's
     aassccttiimmee(), which ends with the four-digit year, followed by
     the time zone name; this places the year immediately before
     the zone name in ddaattee's output, rather than after it as in
     some other systems' date commands.
